<title>USA: Maxwell House revises its coffee increase.</title>
<headline>Maxwell House revises its coffee increase.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maxwell House Coffee Co, a division of Philip Morris Cos Inc, said it revised its increase on the list price of its standard 13-ounce can of coffee to 60 cents from the 45-cent increase announced Feb 21.</p>
<p>This reflects the price of green coffee on the world's futures markets, the company said.</p>
<p>The increase, which takes effect March 31, brings the price for a standard can to $2.86, the company said.</p>
</text>
